1. Open the examiner's repo on GitHub, click the green Code button and copy the link. (If it is not
your repo, click Fork first and copy your fork's link.)
SCREENSHOT 1: Browser - the examiner's repo page on GitHub
2. Run in terminal (put the real link and the repo folder name):
cd ~/Desktop
git clone PASTE_REPO_LINK_HERE
cd REPO_NAME
code .
git log --oneline
git remote -v
SCREENSHOT 2: VS Code - Explorer panel with the cloned files + clone output in terminal
3. In VS Code edit README.md - add a line Updated by Arth Sinha - and save. Create a new file
CHANGELOG.md with the text Added contributor details.
4. Run in terminal:
git status
git diff
git add .
git commit -m "Update README and add CHANGELOG"
git log -1 --stat
git push
SCREENSHOT 3: VS Code terminal - git status showing modified README.md and new
CHANGELOG.md
SCREENSHOT 4: VS Code terminal - git log -1 --stat output
5. Refresh the repo on GitHub - your commit and new file are visible.
SCREENSHOT 5: Browser - GitHub repo page showing your commit and CHANGELOG.md
